# Element indexing an **inferred** variable: `value[0]` states no width, so the
# access is as wide as whatever type inference lands on -- and inference lands
# on the narrowest type under which the program is *provable*. Storing 300 and
# proving it reads back rules out `u8`/`i8` (they truncate it to 44, so the
# `require` fails and the candidate is rejected) and settles on `u16`, which the
# emitted program shows as a 2-byte `sh`/`lhu` and 2 bytes of `.bss`.
#
# This is what byte slices cannot express: `value[0:4]` would have *told* the
# verifier the width, pinning `u32` before inference began.
value: global _
t0 = &value
t1 = 300
t0[0] = t1
t2 = t0[0]
a0 = 300
require t2 == a0
exit(0)
